          <msContents>
            <summary><p>De cura naturali febrium putridarum... in 7th capitulum, tractatus 2, fen prima, libri 4i Avicennae. [Followed by] FRIGIMELICA [or FRIZIMELICA] (Francesco) Varii tractatus. The tracts by F. Frigimelica [1491-1559] are: 'De modo purgandi'. 'De Syrupis'. 'In nono Rasis ad Almansorem lectura' ['De apoplexia'. 'De phrenetide'. 'De pleuritide'.] 'De morbo gallico'. 'De vulneribus capitis'. </p>
              <p>With Frigimelica's work on the Morbus gallicus, of which only part is included, are excertps from the 'De morbo gallico' of Joannes Baptista Montanus [1498-1552]. Both these are printed in full in the 1728 edition of 'Aphrodisiacus' by Aloysius Luisinus.</p></summary>
            <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_183_1">
              <author></author>
              <title type="original">Cassanus (Ferdinandus)</title>
              <textLang mainLang="la" source="IANA"></textLang>
              <note>Dates of the works conjectured to be c.1650 and c.1600 respectively. </note>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
